%% Proactive Scheduled Tasks offline-credentials consent.
%% Separate from both the OIDC login flow (03-login-flow.mmd) and the
%% reactive toolset/external-service sign-in interrupt (08-toolset-signin-
%% interrupt.mmd) — this flow is triggered by route entry into Scheduled
%% Tasks, not by a DIAL-Core-pushed client-channel event mid-completion.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as React SPA
    participant BFF as NestJS BFF
    participant CORE as DIAL Core
    participant IDP as OAuth Provider

    U->>SPA: Navigates to a Scheduled Tasks route
    SPA->>BFF: GET /api/v1/offline-credentials
    BFF->>CORE: GET /v1/user/offline-credentials
    CORE-->>BFF: { available: true, connected: false, connect: {...} }
    BFF-->>SPA: 200 { available: true, connected: false, connect: {...} }

    SPA->>U: Shows "log in required" modal
    U->>SPA: Clicks "Log in"
    SPA->>SPA: Opens same-origin popup synchronously
    SPA->>IDP: Navigates popup to connect.authorizationEndpoint

    U->>IDP: Authenticates and consents (offline_access scope)
    IDP-->>SPA: Redirects popup to ROUTES.ToolsetSignIn?code=...

    SPA->>BFF: POST /api/v1/offline-credentials/signin<br/>{ code, redirectUri }
    BFF->>CORE: POST /v1/user/offline-credentials/signin<br/>{ code, redirectUri }
    CORE-->>BFF: true
    BFF-->>SPA: 200 { success: true }
    SPA->>SPA: Popup reports success over BroadcastChannel, closes

    Note over SPA,CORE: The callback's own reported result is a hint,<br/>not authoritative — the opener always re-verifies.
    SPA->>BFF: GET /api/v1/offline-credentials (authoritative refetch)
    BFF->>CORE: GET /v1/user/offline-credentials
    CORE-->>BFF: { available: true, connected: true }
    BFF-->>SPA: 200 { available: true, connected: true }
    SPA->>U: Modal closes — scheduled tasks can now run unattended
